<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Flintshire</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Flintshire is a county in north-east <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wales">Wales</a> on the southern shore of the Dee estuary, bordering <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, with its administrative centre at Mold. It was created in 1284 by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/statute-of-rhuddlan">Statute of Rhuddlan</a> after Edward I's conquest of Wales, and Flint Castle was one of his first Welsh fortresses. Lead and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coal">coal</a> mining and later heavy industry shaped its economy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/flintshire.jpg" alt="Flintshire" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jeff Buck · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:View_from_Waen_y_Llyn_Country_Park_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3257293.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
